    "turn_text": "One of the things that you're known for as a member of Congress, the National Journal, which we'll talk about a little bit, regularly ranks members of Congress based on their partisanship. They give everybody a partisanship score. There were 435 members of the U.S. House of Representatives, and you regularly came up to 18. Right in the middle. Which means sometimes you go to where the Democrats sometimes go to. Give me one example when you broke away from the Democratic Party and what the Reid would",
