    "turn_text": "Here's what I try to do in the book to address all of these issues. And I think what is unique is I was always sort of a political science geek. And I think you are too. We've read these books that outline the problems and talk about the social science research. And I have a lot in the book about social science research into the way partists think. How people react in group dynamics Will they accept information that conclusively proves their point of view is wrong? They're just factually inaccurate if you present them with that. Anyone want to take a guess if they accept that? No, they do not. How they react, you know, you do brain scans on people and put them under MRIs and show them political information in what parts of the brain like that. Really cool stuff like that. I'm into that stuff. Then you talk about the systemic problems that lead to polarization. gerrymandering, money in politics, the partisan",
