    "turn_idx": 79,
    "turn_text": "number of turnover just in this session. But in just the last 10 years, the amount of turnover in Congress is a record level. So they don't have term limits, but they've replaced the people who leave. And the problem is what we talked about, this is the biggest issue with term limits. You're going to replace somebody with another person who's accountable to those same extremes that the first person was. So when you leave office, you put a different face in there, but they still have to win election by appealing to those same extremes. And it actually makes the problem worse. So, good point. Liz, did you have a question? Go ahead.",
