  {
    "episode_id": 49972,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49972.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 148,
    "turn_text": "Well, at some level, that's what the top two primary does because you have to have a system of winnowing. Otherwise, if you just, everybody went to one and we used to be crowd, then somebody can win 12% of the vote and win. So I think the idea is we want a majority of those voting, as opposed to majority of those voting at least choosing their representative.",
