  {
    "episode_id": 49972,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49972.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 162,
    "turn_text": "I would have said the money part, and even though everyone understands money dominates politics, I don't think people really understand the time that it takes away. I could say something altruistic, like most members of Congress, I think a misconception is people will say, why doesn't anybody know anything about business that's there? Most members of congress forget about the partisanship and the reason they're partisan is because they're accountable. They're more partisan than they would like to be. But most members are high achievers. They're people who are very successful in whatever industry they came from. They could be doing other things and most of them are there for the right reasons. they're just forced to be more partisan than they would like to be, and more angry and confrontational than they would like to be, because of what I said that the extremes dominate the electoral process.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
