    "turn_idx": 165,
    "turn_text": "I've been on this bookstore, so I spoke in Gainesville at the Bob Graham Center, which is awesome when they do amazing work and we had a great time. But a guy approached me afterwards and he represented a group called Fire Your Congressman. And he came up. He said, I would like to talk to you. I'd like for you to run against. I live in Jacksonville now. And the congressman there is a guy named John Rutherford, who I'm friends with. He said, I want you to run against John Rutherford because I'm trying to field a candidate in every race in the country to get rid of every congressman. And I said, why do you want to do that? And he's just frustrated. He's a smart guy. He's a professor at the university. His wife's a professor. He's not a crank. He's a good guy. And I said, well, let me ask you a question, though. Let's say I went. What are you going to do next time? So we're going to take you out. And I said, that doesn't sound so appealing to me. I don't like that.",
